  "implementation_choices": [
    "PreparedPublic owns a canonical immutable public value and its serialized form. It parses/validates the input, then serializes the canonical records to preserve field traversal order even for mutable or reordered structurally equivalent input dataclasses.",
    "Each encoder/writer receives its own mutable wire copy. Exact object identity prevents using a prepared owner for an equal but different decision.",
    "Only the current adapter frame and current rollout encoding retain the owner. Reset, consumed frames, encoding failures and collection cleanup release the relevant ownership; nonterminal cutoffs retain their actual final public decision.",
    "The exact built-in full-run encoder opts into preparation. Custom subclasses keep their encode/pack/ready-wire hooks and validating fallback. Standard full-run and combat PPO recorders receive the prepared owner explicitly.",
    "Prepared recording reuses only the already-validated successor. Action membership/equality, sequence, reconciled execution, reward, completion, digest and atomic no-clobber publication checks remain shared with the original path.",
    "Disk loaders and standalone unprepared inputs still validate independently. No wire-schema, game-rule, guard, RNG, model, mask, reward, optimizer or worker-scheduling change."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One host and seed schedule, three fresh repetitions per build. OS caches and background load uncontrolled.",
    "Profiler times include instrumentation; cumulative rows overlap. Profiled runs are excluded from throughput medians.",
    "50k estimate is a linear extrapolation excluding evaluation/export, not a fresh 50k learning experiment.",
    "Parent peak RSS excludes collector processes. No total-pool memory reduction is claimed.",
    "Inference bundle format remains unchanged. Exact optimizer/RNG resume still requires matching source and runtime."
  ],
